CORE PRINCIPLE — TRUST THE EMPIRICAL PASS RATE, NOT YOUR INTUITION ABOUT DIFFICULTY.
The single most common and most costly mistake is over-confidence: reporting 0.90+ on tasks that "look trivial" but actually fail, or 0.80+ on moderate tasks. The reported pass rate already accounts for how easy the task looks. Do NOT add an upward nudge just because a task seems simple, short, or like basic knowledge.

Reasoning procedure (keep it to one or two sentences):
1. Identify the example group whose CATEGORY, format, and required skills most resemble the target. Read off its empirical pass rate. That rate is your anchor.
2. Set your probability AT that rate. Only adjust if there is a specific, articulable reason — and adjustments should be small (±0.10 at most) and are more often DOWNWARD than upward.

WHEN TO ADJUST DOWNWARD (these are common; apply readily):
- The task requires an EXACT string / exact command / exact format answer (e.g. "complete this command", "give the bash command", short-answer fill-in). These are format-sensitive and fail more often than they look — never report above ~0.80 for such tasks even if the matched rate is 95%+, because the model can know the answer yet phrase it in a non-matching way.
- The task is at the harder end of its group, involves multi-step exploitation, an interactive service, or a specific trick with no obvious path.

WHEN TO ADJUST UPWARD (rare; apply cautiously, never above ~0.90):
- Only for a pure multiple-choice factual question with an unambiguous single correct choice, where the matched group already has a high pass rate.

Calibration guidance (map matched pass rate → reported probability), then apply the adjustments above:
- Matched pass rate ~95–100% → report ~0.85 (not higher, because even "easy" tasks fail).
- Matched pass rate ~80–90% → report ~0.75.
- Matched pass rate ~60–75% → report ~0.62.
- Matched pass rate ~40–55% → report ~0.47.
- Matched pass rate ~25–40% → report ~0.33.
- Matched pass rate ~15–25% → report ~0.20.
- Matched pass rate ~5–15% → report ~0.10.
- Matched pass rate ~0–5% → report ~0.05.
Interpolate between these. Never report above 0.90 or below 0.03. Exact-match / command-completion tasks are capped at 0.80 regardless of matched rate.

Set p50 to your best-estimate probability. Set p25 and p75 to a narrow band around it (typically p50 ± 0.05 to ±0.08), clipped to [0.03, 0.95].

Do not deliberate at length. Keep your rationale to one or two short sentences. Report three percentiles using EXACTLY this format:

<rationale>
Your rationale here.
</rationale>

