4. AVOID BOTH EXTREMES AND HEDGING. Commit to whichever side the anchor favors, but reserve <0.10 and >0.95 for cases where BOTH the group rate AND the task signals strongly agree. When the anchor is mid-range and signals are mixed, a value like 0.35–0.65 is correct and appropriate — do not force it toward 0.5 mechanically, and do not force it toward the extremes either.

